cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ReactionFlow in research, cite this software and the interatomic
  potentials and external codes used in your workflow.
title: "ReactionFlow: automated reaction discovery and pathway refinement for atomistic trajectories"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ellis
    given-names: Austin
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  ReactionFlow finds reactions in molecular dynamics and computes their pathways.
  It watches the bonds while a trajectory runs. When a bond forms or breaks and
  stays that way, it refines the minimum-energy path of that change with NEB and
  climbing-image NEB, using the same machine-learned interatomic potential as the
  dynamics. For reactions too rare to see in molecular dynamics, it runs adaptive
  kinetic Monte Carlo with EON.
keywords:
  - reaction discovery
  - molecular dynamics
  - machine-learned interatomic potentials
  - nudged elastic band
  - transition states
  - adaptive kinetic Monte Carlo
  - reaction mechanisms
repository-code: "https://github.com/Austin243/ReactionFlow"
